<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="mlc">
  <title>Mathematics Learning Center (MLC)</title>

  <p>
    Free math tutoring, online via Zoom or face to face in Heafey 223, is
    available through the Mathematics Learning Center. You can set up a
    one-to-one appointment, sign up for a weekly study group, or come to a
    power up session to strengthen a specific skill. Students need to register
    ahead for these services.
  </p>

  <figure xml:id="fig-mlc">
    <caption>Tutoring at the MLC, one-to-one or in a small study group.</caption>
    <image source="mlc-tutoring.png" width="80%">
      <shortdescription>A tutor at a whiteboard explaining a surface and its contour lines to three students</shortdescription>
      <description>
        <p>
          A cartoon of a tutor standing at a whiteboard, gesturing toward a
          sketch of a hill-shaped surface in three-dimensional axes. A gold
          arrow rises from the high point of the surface, and the contour lines
          of the hill are drawn in the plane below it. Three students sit around
          a round table taking notes, one of them sketching the same contour
          lines in a notebook, with a laptop, books, and a coffee cup on the
          table.
        </p>
      </description>
    </image>
  </figure>

  <p>
    For quick last-minute questions, try drop-in tutoring from 6 to 8 PM on
    Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday evenings.
  </p>
</section>
